# Game metadata is one snapshot, one signal

Team names/colors, competition, date, and abbreviations are a single game-setup snapshot. Mutators (`setGameTeams`, `setGameMetadata`, `clearGameMetadata`) normalize, compare, write, then emit **`gameMetadataChanged()` once** if anything in that call actually changed. Do not add per-field signals.

`tagsChanged()` is only for tag membership/order/counts. Do not piggy-back metadata refreshes on it. `clear()` does not clear metadata; `MainWindow::resetTagSession()` calls `clear()` then `clearGameMetadata()`, so observers must handle the metadata signal or they keep stale team labels after tags are gone.

```cpp
// BAD — UI refreshes on tagsChanged while metadata is written with no signal
tagSession_->clear();
tagSession_->clearGameMetadata();  // silent; stats/game controls still show old names

// GOOD
void TagSession::setGameTeams(...) {
  // trim, compare, assign
  emit gameMetadataChanged();
}
connect(tagSession_, &TagSession::gameMetadataChanged, this, [this]() {
  gameControls_->setSessionTeamNames(tagSession_->homeTeamName(), ...);
  rebuildTagsList();
});
```

Connect observers to existing refresh helpers (`setSessionTeamNames`, `rebuildTagsList`, `updateTeamFilterButtonLabels`, `refreshFromSession`). Exporters read metadata on demand and do not need the signal.
